/* Reserving range 110000-119999 */
/*****************************************
*   5th Level - Arcane - 115500-115999   *
*****************************************/
//Animal Summoning II
@115500 = ~Wand of Animal Summoning II~
/*
Animal Summoning II
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 5
Sphere: Animal, Summoning
Range: 30 ft.
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

By means of this spell, the caster calls from 1 to 3 animals that have 8 Hit Dice or less. The animals summoned aid the caster by whatever means they possess, staying until the spell duration expires. Only normal or giant animals can be summoned; fantastic animals or monsters cannot be summoned by this spell (no chimerae, dragons, gorgons, manticores, etc.).
*/

// Search and replacement strings for Animal Summoning II wand description, which would yield a desired %flavor_text% for
//  The template string (@100003 in `wands-defaults.tra`)
@115502 = ~this spell~   //Search
@115503 = ~this wand~    //replace
@115504 = ~the caster~   //Search
@115505 = ~the wielder~  //replace
@115506 = ~the spell~    //Search
@115507 = ~the effect~   //replace

//I would still need to parse the entire spell description to extract the relevant variables for the template
//  Name, spell school, Level, sphere, range, duration, AoE, and saving throw would be easy to parse.
//  I could read the description myself and allow overrides for the various stat blocks, I suppose.

// Maybe a function to read the Spell Name, Spell School, Level, Sphere, Damage, Range, Duration, AoE, and Saving Throw from the spell description and return them?
//  Then I could allow for manual replacements for the stats if duration or range are variable, for example.
//  I'd then allow a certain number of strings for replacing the flavor text, like above.

// I suppose that could work, but then there would be a huge array of possible STRREFs used for each wand description.
// "It would be better to just write custom descriptions for each wand, I think." is the LLM suggested text, lol.
